From 0000000000000000000000000000000000000000 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Daniel Vicory <dvicory@gmail.com>
Date: Mon, 27 Jul 2026 12:00:00 +0000
Subject: [PATCH] feat(kanban): journal hashless broker workspace handoffs

Represent completion, inheritance, import, and delivery facts as hidden events
in Hermes' existing task-event schema. Do not persist broker workspace, lease,
handoff, export, or hash authority in Hermes; exact-run intents make broker
capture and import replayable before reclaim without exposing internal ids to
models or activity readers.

Validate completion as an immutable tuple of relative artifacts, metadata, and
created cards. Native files enter existing attachment storage before cleanup;
broker selections are preflighted beneath output/ before the writer fence and
delivered from frozen bytes rather than live paths or prose discovery.

Keep generic Kanban persistence, board-qualified recovery, artifact validation,
and transport-neutral control primitives here. The following integration patch
owns plugin registration, notifier delivery, and model-facing tool behavior.
